-- title:
--   Relative q-Frobenius as a semilinear automorphism of the model
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a finite field, $q = \#k$, let $K$ be an algebraically closed field, and let $F_0$ be a field over $k$ and $F$ a field over $K$ and over $F_0$, with `IsCurveOver K F`: every nonzero element of $F$ is the divisor of a degree-zero divisor supported on the places of $F$ over $K$, each place has residue field finite over $K$, and $\Omega_{F/K}$ is free of rank one over $F$. Assume the $K$-intermediate field of $F$ generated by the image of $F_0$ is all of $F$, and let $\varphi \colon F \to F$ be a $K$-algebra endomorphism such that $F$ is integral over the image and $\varphi(x) = x^q$ for $x$ in the image of $F_0$. Let $M$ be a curve model of $F$ over $K$: an integral scheme $M.C$ with proper, smooth of relative dimension one structure morphism $M.\mathrm{toBase} \colon M.C \to \operatorname{Spec} K$, an isomorphism of $F$ with the function field of $M.C$ compatible with $K$, and a bijection from the closed points of $M.C$ onto the places of $F$ over $K$ matching stalks with valuation rings, every finite set of points lying in an affine open. Then there is a ring endomorphism $\sigma$ of $K$ with $\sigma(c) = c^q$ for all $c$, and an isomorphism $B \colon M.C \cong M.C$ such that $B$ followed by $M.\mathrm{toBase}$ followed by $\operatorname{Spec}(\sigma)$ equals $M.\mathrm{toBase}$, and for every $K$-point $y \colon \operatorname{Spec} K \to M.C$ over $\operatorname{Spec} K$ the composite $\operatorname{Spec}(\sigma)$ followed by $y$ followed by $B$ is again such a $K$-point and corresponds, under the bijection `pointEquivPlace` between $K$-points and places, to the restriction along $\varphi$ of the place corresponding to $y$, that is, to the place whose valuation ring is the $\varphi$-preimage of the valuation ring of $y$.
--
--   This is the geometric form, on a smooth proper model, of the statement that the relative $q$-Frobenius of $F = K\cdot F_0$ is a $\sigma$-semilinear automorphism of the model inducing $v \mapsto \varphi^{-1}(\mathcal{O}_v)$ on places. It is used in the construction of the semilinear map on degree-zero Picard data attached to pushforward along Frobenius, in [`AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.exists_semilinear_hom_of_pushforwardAlong_frobenius_of_representsRelSubPic`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Pic0.exists_semilinear_hom_of_pushforwardAlong_frobenius_of_representsRelSubPic).
